                <pb facs="0739" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg677"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Official telegrams</hi>.</head>
                <p rendition="#center">(Sent from Camargo April 27, 1878.)</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To the Minister of War:</p>
                <p>General Cuellar last night sent me the following telegram:</p>
                <p>“The Lerdists have moved from Brownsville: they will cross to-morrow; their plan
                    is to strike a blow—Salinas moving for this purpose from wherever he may be to
                    help them in the operation of the Sierrita (small range of mountains); another
                    party will also move from Davis, down the stream. I have issued the necessary
                    orders.”</p>
                <p>I communicate it to you for your information.</p>
                <closer><signed>SERVANDO CANALES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
